  "raw_label": "1",
  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Kouthavarapu Nammaiah, vs The State Of Ap on 13 September, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.5153 Of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A1 to A5 seek to quash the proceedings against them in C.C.No.342 of 2019 on the file of II Additional Judicial First Class Magistrate, Tenali, which was taken cognizance for the offences under Sections 420, 272, 273, 188 r/w 34 of IPC and Sections 57, 58, 59 and 63 of Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 30.11.2018 around 11.30 hours, when the complainant along with his staff conducting vehicle check on Burripalem road near Sri Vijayalakshmi Dal Mill, intercepted one auto rickshaw and apprehended A2 and A3 and on enquiry, they revealed that they are transporting banned tobacco products on the instructions given by A1 and A4 and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.305 of 2018 of Tenali Rural Police Station, for the offences stated supra. 3. Learned counsel for petitioners while denying the FIR allegations would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act. He relied upon the order of this Court in Crl.P.Nos.3731 of 2018 and batch, dated 27.08.2018.",
